                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "133437451",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198109323439",
                            "num_reviews": 321,
                            "playtime_forever": 361,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 358,
                            "last_played": 1677256100
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Graphic adventure, puzzle, minimal game.\n\nI'm sorry to badmouth a game, but no matter how hard I tried to complete this adventure, I couldn't.\nThe graphics are simple, sparse with few details, while the playability is bad, there are no arrows to show you where to turn and move in the locations, sometimes I discover by chance by clicking around that there are other angles that can be visited.\nObjects are not highlighted if you can interact with them by hovering over them, so sometimes you get stuck wondering what to do.\n\nThe plot is without logic because you wake up with no memory and apart from a few recalled memories, you find yourself escaping from a prison where strangely there is no one and you can access everything: material, codes, cars and flee to the city where even there is desert and you can get what you need at the supermarket, and then go to the Police Station and use their Computers as you like, even accessing their personal files.\n\nThe puzzles are really hard I tried to check Setting there is a section to get suggestions, but as soon as I check it literally crashes the game!\nThe music is quite suitable for the game.\n\nIt's quite frustrating as an experience I got halfway through the game and the objects that should be combined together don't work so I can't continue, my advice is to forget it and dedicate yourself to something else ....\n\n\n[quote]For more puzzle game reviews, news and everything puzzle-related, follow [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/25928931-Puzzle-Lovers/]Puzzle Lovers[/url] and check out our [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/puzzlelovers]Steam group[/url].[/quote]\n\n",
